  "id": "Compound::DB00768 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Olopatadine, a histamine H1 receptor antagonist, is linked to Cyp3a4 through multiple pathways that converge on the histamine-1 receptor antagonsim class. The evidence suggests that Olopatadine, along with its analogs Azelastine and Carbinoxamine, binds to the same biological class, which includes organic heterocyclic compounds. This class is associated with the inhibition of Cyp3a4, a key enzyme in drug metabolism. The lowest common ancestor of these compounds points to the histamine-1 receptor antagonsim class, reinforcing the shared mechanism of action. The integration of these pathways implies that Olopatadine may modulate Cyp3a4 through a common mechanism, possibly involving the inhibition of histamine release or direct interaction with the enzyme. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Olopatadine and Cyp3a4, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
